    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While I understand your desire to manage this at home, the use of combination or extended-release NSAIDs such as ibuprofen with a higher dosage (like 800 mg) every few hours is not recommended without clear instructions from a healthcare professional. High doses of ibuprofen can increase the risk of serious side effects, including gastrointestinal bleeding, kidney damage, and other adverse effects. Stick to the recommended dosage on the label. If you've already taken more than what's prescribed, it's important to contact a healthcare provider as soon as possible to discuss your symptoms and the use of over-the-counter medication.\n\nMonitor your symptom carefully. If you develop severe symptoms, like uncontrollable pain, severe swelling, signs of a heart attack (such as severe pain in the middle or upper body, extreme shortness of breath, cold sweat, nausea, or light-headedness), or signs of a gastrointestinal bleed (like dark stools, vomiting blood, or severe and sudden stomach pain), seek emergency care immediately. Your well-being is the ultimate priority, and a healthcare professional can provide safe guidance on how to manage your symptoms without unnecessary risk.",
